ction(){location.href='/results/' + $('#same_games_select').val();})"]] " | " [:form {:class "form-inline form-inline-header"} [:select {:name "id", :id "other_games_select", :class "form-control"} [:option {:value ""} "In other Games"] "\n" [:option {:value "185005"} "1912"] "\n" [:option {:value "185026"} "1920"] "\n" [:option {:value "185045"} "1924"] "\n" [:option {:value "185082"} "1932"] "\n" [:option {:value "185099"} "1936"] "\n" [:option {:value "185118"} "1948"] "\n" [:option {:value "185135"} "1952"] "\n" [:option {:value "185153"} "1956"] "\n" [:option {:value "185176"} "1960"]] [:script {} "$('#other_games_select').change(function(){location.href='/results/' + $('#other_games_select').val();})"]] " | " [:a {:href "/event_names/264"} "Event type"]] [:h1 {:class "event_title"} "Individual, Men" [:small {}]] [:table {:class "biodata"} [:tbody {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Date"] [:td {} "8 – 11 August 1928"]] [:tr {} [:th {} "Status"] [:td {} "Olympic"]] [:tr {} [:th {} "Location"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/venues/285"} "Olympisch Stadion, Amsterdam"] " / " [:a {:href "/venues/289"} "Sportpark, Hilversum"] " / " [:a {:href "/venues/290"} "Maartensdijkse Bos, Hilversum"]]] [:tr {} [:th {} "Participants"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/events/185063"} "46 from 17 countries"]]] [:tr {} [:th {} "Format"] [:td {:colspan "2"} "Dressage, cross-country, and jumping."]] [:tr {} [:th {:valign "top"} "Details"] [:td {} "Maximum Points: 2,000"]]]] [:div {:class "description"} [:p {} "The three-day event came down to Dutch riders who took three of the top four places, with only Germany’s " [:a {:href "/athletes/12488"} "Bruno Neumann"] ", who won bronze, breaking up their monopoly. The leader after the dressage was " [:a {:href "/athletes/11827"} "Gerard de Kruijff"] ", just ahead of his teammate " [:a {:href "/athletes/12534"} "Charles Pahud de Mortanges"] ". In the endurance phase, neither was among the top leaders, but Pahud de Mortanges moved into a narrow lead going into the jumping. Both Dutch riders had a perfect score of 300.0 in the jumping phase, which allowed Pahud de Mortanges to maintain his lead and win the gold medal. He would return in " [:a {:href "/results/185082"} "1932"] " and defend his gold medal in Los Angeles, and would compete again in " [:a {:href "/results/185099"} "Berlin"] ", but would not finish the event. Both he and de Kruijff had competed at Paris in 1924, winning gold medals in the " [:a {:href "/results/185068"} "team three-day event"] ". De Kruijff rode " [:a {:href "/horses/2596"} [:em {} "Va-t-en"]] " in 1928, who belonged to Pahud de Mortanges, as de Kruijff’s regular horse, " [:em {} "Kakkerlak"] ", was injured shortly before the Amsterdam Olympics."] "\n\n" [:p {} "Pahud de Mortanges had an interesting life. In 1938, he sustained a serious wrist injury, almost causing his hand to be amputated. In 1942, he was taken as a prisoner-of-war, but escaped in 1943 by jumping out of a train and travelling to Gibraltar. He took part in the Normandy landings as a major, and was later made Chief of H. M. Military House from 1954-62. He was also President of the Dutch NOC in 1946-51 and 1959-64."] "\n"] [:table {:class "table table-striped"} [:thead {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Pos"] [:th {} "Number"] [:th {} "Competitor"] [:th {} "Horse"] [:th {} "NOC"] [:th {} "Points"] [:th {}] [:th {}] [:th {}]]] [:tbody {} [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "1"] [:td {:class "bib"} "–"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/12534"} "Charles Pahud de Mortanges"]] [:td {} [:i {} [:a {:href "/horses/1570"} "Marcroix"]]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/NED"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/NED.png"}] "NED"]] [:td {} "1,969.82"] [:td {} [:span {:class "Gold"} "Gold"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "2"] [:td {:class "bib"} "–"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/11827"} "Gerard de Kruijff"]] [:td {} [:i {} [:a {:href "/horses/2596"} "Va-t-en"]]] [:td {} [